      "description": "VHT is a device for welding, cutting and soldering metals and spraying coatings in open space. Created in the 1980s. at the E. O. Paton Electric Welding Institute.\n\nThe tool is placed in a container 40x45x50 cm in size and weighing 30 kg. The VHT has its own power source and is an autonomous backpack-type vehicle that can be carried behind the back or fixed on the surface of the orbital station. The working head weighing 3.5 kg has the shape of a pistol, the handle of which is adjusted to the size of the suit glove. The “pistol” contains a double-barreled electron gun with an accelerating voltage of 5 kV and a power consumption of 1 kW. One barrel is used for cutting and welding metals, the other is for spraying the coating from a special container.\n\nVHT was used by S. Savitskaya and V. Dzhanibekov at the Salyut-7 orbital station - they welded metal in open space for 3 hours. Later VHT transported to the Mir station."
    },
